# Milestone: v0.10.11-channel-and-isA
# Covers: closure capture from definition scope, not call scope; 'var Object.f'
#         slot assignment on a prototype; lookup of i inside f() resolves to
#         outer global i, not inner block-local i.
# blocked: needs a `## host:` body.  The host driver has existed since
# the core re-foundation (tests/integration/chk_host_driver.c) -- what is
# missing is this fixture, rewritten to drive its own clock and its own
# urbi_step calls.  That is per-fixture authoring work, scheduled with the
# rest of the corpus in Phase 5.  The annotation it replaced said the
# driver did not exist, which stopped being true at Task 12.
# matrix-row: object-slot-install
#
# Reason:
#   Object readonly was blocked by D5 prior to v0.10.11; resolved at W5
#   (Object atom proto unfrozen).  `var Object.f = ...` now works.
#   Remaining block is the T39 chk driver: the expected output line
#   `[00000002:error] !!! input.u:4.31: lookup failed: i` requires the
#   T39 multi-line driver to match error output lines embedded among the
#   expected-value sequence.  The core closure-captures-definition-scope
#   semantic is verified at M3 via tests/chk/closure/counter.chk;
#   Object slot-install works post-v0.10.11.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when T39 chk driver lands):
